AUDIT CONCLUSION: the tail of _agr1_train evaluates the same expression on the same folds twice. The second walk is 6 calls per layer (2 roles x 3 folds) out of 204 total, and every one of them returns a bit-identical scalar that the loop already had.
The reusable per-fold scalars are the two `_agr1_scale_loss_grad(...)[0]` values the final_loss loop already computes for m and p; the ratios are their fold sums divided by len(prepared), and the loop's own per-fold values are summed in the same order the ratio expressions use.
DUPLICATION CONFIRMED -- an implementation card is warranted.
